    "text": "Boudicca is a queen of the Iceni in the south-east of Britain. After the loss of her family and the wrongs she suffered, she rose against Roman power. She summoned the war goddess Andraste at her last hour. The rising did not hold, and she took her own life. The name Boudicca is Celtic and means the victorious woman. The common spelling Boadicea rests on no certain ancient source. The Welsh form of the name is Buddug. Gildas knew of her revolt but did not name her, calling her only the lioness. Beda and Geoffrey of Monmouth do not speak of her.",
